 "answer": "The earliest 2024 paper in the index is **“Large Language Model based Multi-Agents: A Survey of Progress and Challenges”** (arXiv:2402.01680), dated **January 21, 2024** in the index. [D1]\n\n- **Main idea:** It surveys systems where multiple LLM-powered agents—with different roles and capabilities—communicate and collaborate on tasks or simulate complex environments. [C1, C2]\n- **Organizing framework:** It breaks these systems into four parts: interaction with the environment, agent profiles, communication, and how agents acquire capabilities. [C4]\n- **Applications:** It groups research into **problem-solving** and **world simulation**, with examples including software development, multi-robot systems, and social or policy simulations. [C3, C4]\n- **Practical value:** It maps the field and collects implementation frameworks, datasets, and benchmarks—a broad orientation to multi-agent AI rather than a paper introducing one new system. [C3, C4]",
